## 📋 CustomerEmailEscalation — Architectural Plan

### What it does

When a support email arrives in your Microsoft Outlook 365 inbox, the flow:
1. **Classifies** it as **High Priority** or **Normal** using a keyword-based script (e.g., "urgent", "outage", "critical", "refund", "fraud")
2. **High-priority path:** instantly alerts your team on Slack → sends an auto-reply promising fast attention → moves the email to an "Urgent" folder
3. **Normal path:** sends a standard acknowledgment → moves the email to a "Normal" folder
4. **Error path:** logs any classification or Slack failures gracefully without crashing

### Flow Diagram

```mermaid
graph LR
    emailTrigger(Email Received Outlook 365)
    classifyEmail[Classify Email Priority]
    isHighPriority{High Priority}
    slackAlert[Slack Alert Support Team]
    replyUrgent[Reply to Customer Urgent]
    moveUrgent[Move to Urgent Folder]
    replyNormal[Reply to Customer Normal]
    moveNormal[Move to Normal Folder]
    handleTriggerError[Log Trigger Error]
    handleSlackError[Log Slack Error]
    doneEscalated(Done Escalated)
    doneNormal(Done Normal)
    doneError(Done Error)
    emailTrigger -->|output| classifyEmail
    classifyEmail -->|success| isHighPriority
    classifyEmail -->|error| handleTriggerError
    isHighPriority -->|true| slackAlert
    isHighPriority -->|false| replyNormal
    slackAlert -->|output| replyUrgent
    slackAlert -->|error| handleSlackError
    replyUrgent -->|output| moveUrgent
    moveUrgent -->|output| doneEscalated
    replyNormal -->|output| moveNormal
    moveNormal -->|output| doneNormal
    handleTriggerError -->|success| doneError
    handleSlackError -->|success| doneError
```

### What's connected to what

| Service | How it's used | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **Microsoft Outlook 365** | Trigger (new email), auto-reply, move to folder | ✅ Connector found, live connection available |
| **Slack** | Alert support team channel on high-priority emails | ✅ Connector found, live connection available |
| **Script node** | Keyword classifier (runs inside the flow, no external service) | ✅ Built-in, no connection needed |

